<%# locals: (item:) %>

<%#
  The row's comment and receipt counts, wrapped so a stream can swap in fresh
  ones, even when a badge is hidden at zero. `contents` keeps the badges direct
  flex items of the memo cell.

  These are the item's cached counts from Ledger::Item#refresh!, which cover
  more than the comments and receipts on its HCB code. Comments also include
  ones shared on a transfer's Disbursement, and admin-only ones for auditors.
  A reimbursement payout counts its expense's receipts.

  Replaced with `turbo_stream.replace [item, :badges]` by:
  - ReceiptsController, when a receipt on the item's HCB code changes
  - CommentsController#destroy, when a comment on the item's HCB code is deleted
  - the transaction popovers, which reload after a comment is posted

  Those changes touch the HCB code, which touches the item and refreshes its
  counts before the stream renders. A comment shared on the Disbursement only
  touches the Disbursement, so the count misses it until something else
  refreshes the item.
%>
<div id="<%= dom_id(item, :badges) %>" class="contents">
  <%= list_badge_for auditor_signed_in? ? item.comment_count : item.not_admin_only_comment_count, "comment", "post", optional: true %>
  <%= list_badge_for item.receipt_count, "receipt", "payment-docs", optional: item.receipt_optional?, required: item.missing_receipt? %>
</div>
